# Regression: old [instance [ClassName Type] methods...] syntax still accepted.
# The parser converts [ClassName Type] to a synthetic PatternDecl internally,
# so legacy syntax produces the same AST as new [pattern [a@Type]] syntax.
[
  Equatable: [class [Equatable a]
    eq: [Fn@Bool [a a]]]

  # Old syntax: class name and type in a single bracket, methods as sibling entries
  EqInt: [instance [Equatable Int]
    eq: [fn [x y] [= x y]]]

  result: true
]

---

%.result
=== out
Bool(true)
